.TH SDL_HINT_WINDOW_FRAME_USABLE_WHILE_CURSOR_HIDDEN 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WINDOW_FRAME_USABLE_WHILE_CURSOR_HIDDEN \- A variable controlling whether the window frame and title bar are interactive when the cursor is hidden.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WINDOW_FRAME_USABLE_WHILE_CURSOR_HIDDEN \(dqSDL_WINDOW_FRAME_USABLE_WHILE_CURSOR_HIDDEN\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: The window frame is not interactive when the cursor is hidden (no move, resize, etc)\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: The window frame is interactive when the cursor is hidden\[char46] (default)
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

